# Explain implementation (cursor-packs)

**CONSTRAINT:** When the agent finishes an implementation or fix that changed project files, or when the user asks what changed / how it was built, MUST Read and follow `.cursor/skills/explain-implementation/SKILL.md` before the final user-facing reply.

- MUST: explain what is different now and how the change is put together, briefly, in plain English.
- MUST NOT: end with only a file list, test status, or “want me to commit?” with no explain.
- MUST NOT: force a fixed heading template or pad with fluff.
- Enforcement: Before send on an implement/fix turn, confirm the skill was applied to the reply draft.
- Violation: STOP, Read the skill, rewrite the reply, then send.

CORRECT:
```text
Edited promote path → short plain-English what + how; no empty section ceremony
```

PROHIBITED:
```text
Edited files → “Done. Tests pass. Commit?”
```

Chat voice remains `.cursor/rules/always-rules-01-human-interaction.mdc`. This rule only requires a useful post-implementation explain, not a rigid format.
